vmvga: compressed volume DMA used pixel rows for the guest slice pitch

SVGAGuestImage.pitch is the distance between rows of blocks, so a slice
of a block-compressed volume texture is ceil(height / block_height) block
rows, not height rows. With the old value every slice after the first
was looked for 4x too far into the guest buffer, past maximumOffset, so
the whole upload of DXTn volume textures (Halo Online's 1024x1024x8
DXT5 volumes) was rejected by the box check.

diff --git a/hw/display/vmware_vga_3d.c b/hw/display/vmware_vga_3d.c
index d079579..2335793 100644
--- a/hw/display/vmware_vga_3d.c
+++ b/hw/display/vmware_vga_3d.c
@@ -9847,7 +9847,12 @@ static bool vmsvga3d_surface_dma_box(struct vmsvga_state_s *s,
         return false;
     }
 
-    guest_plane_pitch = (uint64_t)image->size.height * guest_pitch;
+    /* The guest pitch is the distance between rows of blocks, so one slice
+     * holds ceil(height / block_height) of them (1/4 of the pixel rows for
+     * DXTn/BCn volume textures). */
+    guest_plane_pitch =
+        (uint64_t)((image->size.height + block_height - 1) / block_height) *
+        guest_pitch;
 
     for (z = 0; z < blocks_z; z++) {
         for (y = 0; y < blocks_y; y++) {
